--- NOTE ON THE KODAK/PAKON SOFTWARE ---

This project contains no Kodak or Pakon code, binaries or firmware. It is an
interoperability layer: it lets the genuine F-X35 COM Server stack, which you
must supply from your own scanner's software, talk to a Pakon F-135 over USB
on macOS.

One exception, stated plainly rather than buried: setup/base-config.reg holds
189 registry settings that are Kodak's configuration, not ours -- the F-135
software's own driver flags and colour-table entries. Kodak's installer would
write them; this project does not run that installer, so it supplies them.
The file is unit-independent by construction: it contains no scanner serial,
type or hardware version, and no DpiBase key, because those are read from each
unit's EEPROM, and no light values, because those are measured by the LED servo
on each machine. Whether TLB will write these settings itself, making the file
unnecessary, is an open question -- see docs/SETUP.md.

Protocol details in docs/ were determined by observing the behaviour of that
software and disassembling it for interoperability purposes only.

server/ezusb_stage2.ihex is the generic Cypress/Anchor EZ-USB second-stage
RAM loader -- the 361-record loader array published in Cypress's EZ-USB
development kit and carried in the open FX35 driver work as the
INTEL_HEX_RECORD loader[361] table in FX35Loader/Loader.c. It is not Kodak
code, is not specific to this scanner, and contains no calibration or
model data. The scanner's own application firmware is never bundled here;
it is uploaded at runtime from a file you supply.
